**PR #6210 fix(a11y): name every virtual keyboard key with its pitch and octave**

### 🎯 What does this PR do?
The on-screen piano announced only C keys by pitch ("C4 (MIDI 60)"); every other key was a bare "MIDI 62", so a screen-reader user could not tell which note a key plays. Every white and black key now announces its pitch name and octave the way C keys already did, through a small shared formatter beside NOTE_NAMES that uses the existing middle-C-is-C4 convention.

### 🧪 How to test
1. Open Sourdaw, press Cmd+Shift+K to open the virtual keyboard, and turn on VoiceOver (Cmd+F5).
2. Move the VoiceOver cursor across the keys around middle C. Each key is read with its pitch: C4 (MIDI 60), C#4 (MIDI 61), D4 (MIDI 62) and so on, black keys included.
3. Press Z or X to shift the octave and move across the keys again. The announced octave follows the keys shown, and the visible C labels are unchanged.

### 📌 Related issues & additional notes
None.

